{"all_found":[],"allowed_cmds":[],"applied":{"adjudicate@0":true,"discover@0":true},"base_sha":"e2ded5bbe1488d4135d8078c745076c96e3a985a","calibration":false,"confirmed":[],"created_at":"2026-09-30T19:09:11.614674Z","findings":[{"category":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The guard accepts a verdict only when the envelope reports num_turns exactly 1 and fails closed (retried, then unparseable) on an absent or zero count, coupling the whole claude-cli transport to one version-dependent envelope field. If an installed claude CLI omits or renames num_turns, every claude-cli judge call burns MaxAttempts and returns a fail-closed verdict with no verdict produced, so reviews routed to claude-cli/ stall - a loud, safe failure but a total outage of that transport.","line":162,"severity":"p2","source":"lens"},{"category":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","issue_text":"[ADVISORY] Hook isolation rests on a single --settings disableAllHooks overlay, and the comment asserts it covers plugin-provided hooks, whereas the codex arm disables hooks and plugins with two separate flags because they are distinct surfaces there. If disableAllHooks does not also neutralize plugin hooks, a plugin hook can still speak in the judge's session and the num_turns backstop only fires if the continuation also bumps the reported turn count.","line":88,"severity":"p2","source":"lens"},{"category":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","issue_text":"[ADVISORY] The fail-closed block (CapText, the Parsed/Decision/Confidence reset, the continued-past message, lastErr=nil) reproduces the codex arm's block rather than sharing one helper. A future change to the fail-closed verdict shape or message must be made in two files; if only one is updated the codex and claude arms silently diverge for the same condition.","line":166,"severity":"p3","source":"lens"},{"category":"advisory","file":"internal/fsm/judge/claude.go","issue_text":"[ADVISORY] T